WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.480
In a deer park near Varanasi, five former
companions in asceticism meet the Buddha

2
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:06.540
again.

3
00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.650
He has just found awakening.

4
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.150
Now he gives his first sermon.

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.720
It sets out four noble truths.

6
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.190
One listener understands at once.

7
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.260
Listen to its four steps,
and something sounds medical.

8
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.080
So why did the Buddha's first sermon
sound like a doctor's diagnosis?

9
00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.090
In this mission, you'll
hear how the sermon opens,

10
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.770
with a middle way between two extremes.

11
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.320
Then you'll unpack each
of the four truths,

12
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.810
and what it asks of a follower.

13
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:41.140
Your mission: explain why the Buddha's first
sermon works like a doctor's diagnosis.
